{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791594493,"nonce":"+G3NK+Gaq6P/vn0uz7BJP18zjdI=","title":"Ports from ashui, in priority order","message":"The user's priority (2026-10-10): the wiki is meaningless without a solid foundation, so port what ashui has and blinc_ts lacks before building on it. This ranks them. Evidence marked (checked) was reproduced in this repo; the rest comes from a survey of ashui by a read-only agent and has not been re-run.\n\nDone\n- Cascade registration: Host.createElement did not describe a plain element to the cascade, so no type, universal or structural selector matched it (checked, fixed, tested in native-css).\n- CSS paint read in Rust and applied natively: colours (hex, names, rgb, hsl, color-mix, currentcolor), gradients, glass with glass-*, transform, filter, mask-image, box-shadow, corner-shape, opacity, visibility, border and outline shorthands and longhands, per-side colours. Replaces the TypeScript parser, which read nine properties and dropped the rest without a word (checked). Landing: see the issue titled \"Land the blinc_abi css-paint branch\".\n- User-agent stylesheet, theme-driven, as blinc_ts/theme/user-agent. Tags are flex rows with no look of their own (checked).\n\nNext, in order\n1. Top layer and anchored placement. Popover, Tooltip, Select, Menu and Dialog need it. TypeScript only.\n2. Motion: a frame and timer scheduler, then CSS transition and @keyframes from the cascade, exit animations, springs. Parses today and does nothing (checked). Tracked in 35f7bd0.\n3. Inline text flow, so p and h1 with nested a, strong and code wrap as one paragraph. Wiki prose depends on it.\n4. Scrollbars (the thumb is never drawn: checked).\n5. Built-in element behaviours: list markers, a[href], label, details, progress, forms.\n6. The interaction states the host never sets: checked, indeterminate, invalid and the rest (checked: the host sets seven).\n7. Remaining paint: clip-path, overflow-fade, backdrop-filter, text-decoration, text-align, url() backgrounds.\n\nLater\n- Reactive JSX runtime and control flow (Show, For, owners): adapters/jsx builds once and has no reactive bindings.\n- img, svg and tinted icons (the renderer already has the mask and tile branches).\n- A UI scene snapshot harness with input scripts and a hit-map overlay.\n- Utility vocabulary and variants (hover:, dark:, group-hover:, ring, gradients).\n- calc() and min/max/clamp in lengths (the engine has none).\n- App runner and window conveniences, IME placement, DOM-style lookups.\n- Vector drawing and charts, which depend on the 2D canvas context in 11ae770.\n\nEach of 1, 3, 4, 5, 6 and 7 has its own issue, filed with this one. ashui files, for structure only, are named in each.","files":null}]}